<title>USA: Shuffle Master buys back $2.5 mln in stock.</title>
<headline>Shuffle Master buys back $2.5 mln in stock.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shuffle Master Inc on Tuesday said it repurchased $2.5 million shares of its common stock, about half the amount authorized under a buyback program begun in November.</p>
<p>More than 275,000 shares were retired as a result of the purchases, the company said.</p>
<p>The casino gaming equipment company said it would make further purchases as market conditions, share availability and liquidity permit.</p>
<p>Shuffle Master shares were unchanged at nine in midafternoon trading.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
